<item>
  <title>How to create a virtual machine using qemu+kvm</title>
  <dc:creator>Jianping Meng</dc:creator>
  <link>https://jpmeng.github.io/virtualcluster/20260502_virtualHPC_generalVM.html</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<section id="host-environment-setup" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="host-environment-setup">Host environment setup</h2>
<p>To create virtual machines using qemu+kvm under Rocky Linux, we need to install the necessary packages and set up the environment.</p>
<p>First, we need to install the required packages and start the libvirt service:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> dnf install <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-y</span> virt-install libvirt qemu-kvm libguestfs-tools</span>
<span id="cb1-2"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> systemctl enable <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--now</span> libvirtd</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>If a personal computer is used, probably not much space is allocated for the /var directory, which is the default location for storing virtual machine images. To avoid running out of space, we can create a directory under /home to store the images and give libvirt/qemu permission to access it:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb2" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb2-1"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">cd</span> /home</span>
<span id="cb2-2"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> mkdir vms</span>
<span id="cb2-3"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> chown <span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$USER</span>:<span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$USER</span> vms</span>
<span id="cb2-4"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> chmod 711 vms</span>
<span id="cb2-5"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># tell selinux to allow libvirt to access the directory and files therein</span></span>
<span id="cb2-6"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> semanage fcontext <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-a</span> <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-t</span> virt_image_t <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"/home/vms(/.*)?"</span></span>
<span id="cb2-7"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># apply the new context to the existing files and directories</span></span>
<span id="cb2-8"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> restorecon <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-R</span> <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-v</span> /home/vms</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Through my test, 711 is minimum permission for the directory /home/vms to allow libvirt to access it. If it is 700, libvirt will complain about permission denied when trying to access the image file in that directory.</p>
<p>For convenience, we can make our own user a member of the libvirt group [1], so that we can manage virtual machines without sudo:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sudo</span> usermod <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-a</span> <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-G</span> libvirt <span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$USER</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>To ensure that the new group membership is effective, we can log out and log back in.</p>
<p>We also need to set the LIBVIRT_DEFAULT_URI environment variable to point to the system-wide libvirt instance <code>qemu:///system</code>. Otherwise, the default is <code>qemu:///session</code> pointing to the user session.</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb4" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb4-1"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">export</span> <span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">LIBVIRT_DEFAULT_URI</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"qemu:///system"</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>We can add the above line to our shell profile (e.g., <code>~/.bashrc</code> or <code>~/.zshrc</code>) to make it permanent.</p>
</section>
<section id="network-setup" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="network-setup">Network setup</h2>
<p>Next, we need to prepare the network for the virtual machines. By default, libvirt provides a NATed network called “default”. We can start it and set it to autostart:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb5" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb5-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">virsh</span> net-start default</span>
<span id="cb5-2"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">virsh</span> net-autostart default</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>If somehow the default network is not available, we can create it using the default XML configuration file provided by libvirt:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb6" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb6-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">virsh</span> net-define /usr/share/libvirt/networks/default.xml</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>At this moment it is sufficient to use the default network for our virtual machines. For more advanced network configuration, please refer to the official documentation [2-3].</p>
</section>
<section id="image-preparation" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="image-preparation">Image preparation</h2>
<p>To prepare the image for the virtual machine, we could take advantage of the cloud image provided by <a href="https://rockylinux.org/download">Rocky Linux</a>, which is a qcow2 image with cloud-init pre-installed.</p>
<p>We can then utilise the <code>virt-customize</code> tool to customize the image, such as setting the password for the root user, creating a test user, and resizing the image to have enough space for the root partition. Below is an example of how to do this:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb7" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb7-1"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># let virt-customize access the image file directly without using libvirt, which is faster and more efficient</span></span>
<span id="cb7-2"><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">VM_NAME</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$1</span></span>
<span id="cb7-3"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">export</span> <span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>direct</span>
<span id="cb7-4"><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"/home/vms"</span></span>
<span id="cb7-5"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># assumming the cloud image is already downloaded to $IMAGE_DIR, and its name is Rocky-9-GenericCloud-Base.latest.x86_64.qcow2</span></span>
<span id="cb7-6"><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">IMAGE</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/Rocky-9-GenericCloud-Base.latest.x86_64.qcow2"</span></span>
<span id="cb7-7"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">cp</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$IMAGE</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$VM_NAME</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.qcow2"</span></span>
<span id="cb7-8"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Resize the image to 40G to have enough space for the root partition</span></span>
<span id="cb7-9"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">qemu-img</span> resize <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$VM_NAME</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.qcow2"</span> 40G</span>
<span id="cb7-10"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Customize the image</span></span>
<span id="cb7-11"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Replace TESTUSER and TESTUSERPASSWORD with your own username and password for the test user</span></span>
<span id="cb7-12"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># The root user will be locked and cannot be used to log in</span></span>
<span id="cb7-13"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">virt-customize</span> <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-a</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$VM_NAME</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.qcow2"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-14">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"passwd -l root"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-15">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"usermod -L root"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-16">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--edit</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'/etc/passwd: s/^root:x:0:0:root:\/root:\/bin\/bash/root:x:0:0:root:\/root:\/sbin\/nologin/'</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-17">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--hostname</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$VM_NAME</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-18">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--password</span> TESTUSER:password:TESTUSERPASSWORD <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-19">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"useradd -m -G wheel TESTUSER"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-20">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--edit</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'/etc/default/grub: s/GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=\"/GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=\"console=tty0 console=ttyS0,115200n8 /'</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-21">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"grub2-mkconfig -o /boot/grub2/grub.cfg"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-22">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'growpart /dev/sda 4 || growpart /dev/sda 3'</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-23">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'xfs_growfs /'</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb7-24">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--uninstall</span> cloud-init <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>In the <code>virt-customize</code> command, the arguments</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb8" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb8-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--edit</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'/etc/default/grub: s/GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=\"/GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=\"console=tty0 console=ttyS0,115200n8 /'</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb8-2">--run-command <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"grub2-mkconfig -o /boot/grub2/grub.cfg"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>are used to enable the serial console, which is necessary for us to access the virtual machine through the serial console later.</p>
<p>The argument</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb9" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb9-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--run-command</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'growpart /dev/sda 4 || growpart /dev/sda 3'</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>tries to grow the partition 4 of the disk /dev/sda, which is the root partition in the cloud image. If it fails (e.g., because there are only 3 partitions), it will try to grow partition 3 instead.</p>
</section>
<section id="virtual-machine-creation" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="virtual-machine-creation">Virtual machine creation</h2>
<p>To create the virtual machine, we can use the <code>virt-install</code> command. Below is an example of how to do this:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb10" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode numberSource bash number-lines code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb10-1"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">export</span> <span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>direct</span>
<span id="cb10-2"><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">VM_NAME</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$1</span></span>
<span id="cb10-3"><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">IMAGE_NAME</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$2</span></span>
<span id="cb10-4"><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"/home/vms"</span></span>
<span id="cb10-5"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">virt-install</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-6">--name <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$VM_NAME</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span> <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-7">--ram 4096 <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-8">--vcpus 2 <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-9">--cpu host-passthrough <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-10">--os-variant rocky9 <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-11">--disk path=<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$IMAGE_DIR</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span><span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">$VM_NAME</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.qcow2"</span>,bus=virtio <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-12">--network network=default <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-13">--import <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-14">--graphics none <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-15">--boot uefi <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">\</span></span>
<span id="cb10-16">--serial pty <span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
